From 9f6b7322ce38a1be815158067d68af74a6825170 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Hades <15710513+hadesdevls@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 24 Nov 2026 18:00:27 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [Hades][dvbridge] The IPT tunnel in the matrices that a
 licensed core sends, profile 5 too

"As licensed players send (IPT)" sent the matrices of the RPUs of profile 5
(YCCtoRGB 8192 799 1681 ..., RGBtoLMS 17081 -349 ...), and only for profiles 7
and 8. A licensed core does neither: Dolby's own core (IDK 2.6) on an Amlogic
player, read on the user's player in TV-led output with five films of profiles
5, 7 and 8.1 (its "reversed md_reg3" dump), sent IPT-PQ-c2 for every film with
the same fixed matrices, a profile 5 title with its own matrices among them:

  YCCtoRGB 2002 031f 0691 2002 fc5b 0443 2002 010b ea57
  offsets  00000000 08000000 08000000
  RGBtoLMS 42b8 fea4 fea4 fea4 42b8 fea4 fea4 fea4 42b8

The first column of YCCtoRGB is 8194, not 8192, and the crosstalk 17080 and
-348, not 17081 and -349. dvbridge_ipt.h now has those, so that the header of
the tunnel is the licensed core's byte for byte, which is what the name of the
choice says. The pass of the tunnel inverts them exactly as before.

A profile 5 picture now goes out in those matrices as well: the pass takes the
picture through its own RPU's RGBtoLMS (dvbridge_source_params::lms_rpu, the
integers of the RPU) instead of that of BT.2020, which is the same chain for
profiles 7 and 8 (their RGBtoLMS is BT.2020's, so their codes change only by the
new matrices) and takes a profile 5 picture from the matrices of its RPU to
those of the tunnel. The serializer takes an ICtCp picture into the tunnel.

Nothing changes with the default transport (as composed).
